1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,590
Iron Web times Voyara.

2
00:00:02,235 --> 00:00:04,490
The intelligence behind every journey.

3
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:07,570
At the heart of Iron Web lies a living memory graph.

4
00:00:07,835 --> 00:00:09,570
Hot context. Context cards.

5
00:00:09,815 --> 00:00:12,550
Durable evidence. All connected in one place.

6
00:00:13,055 --> 00:00:14,130
Open any memory.

7
00:00:14,275 --> 00:00:18,750
And the inspector reveals its values, its history, and the sources behind
it.

8
00:00:20,995 --> 00:00:22,670
Nine actors are registered in the system.

9
00:00:22,895 --> 00:00:26,470
For this planning workflow, seven specialists collaborate with a memory
orchestrator.

10
00:00:26,795 --> 00:00:29,140
The activity timeline brings their work to life.

11
00:00:29,155 --> 00:00:32,390
Select an event and see exactly what happened.

12
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:37,220
Bounded instructions and traveler facts, task-specific context cards, and
durable evidence that can be

13
00:00:37,235 --> 00:00:38,310
retrieved when it matters.

14
00:00:38,615 --> 00:00:42,800
With Context X-ray, you can look inside each agent's captured input, see
how context was allocated, which

15
00:00:42,815 --> 00:00:45,170
fields were supported, and which claims connect back to their sources.

16
00:00:45,595 --> 00:00:49,110
The cache reveals measured reuse, payload sizes, and entry limits.

17
00:00:49,555 --> 00:00:53,050
The provider view displays recorded requests and reported model token
usage.

18
00:00:53,555 --> 00:00:56,920
Hardware monitoring distinguishes observed memory from GPU utilization that
isn't available.

19
00:00:56,935 --> 00:01:01,290
Latency points reveal measured context assembly and agent execution time.

20
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:06,010
You can inspect live databases, Qdrant vectors, execution receipts, and
masked provider identities.

21
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:12,200
Filters Keyboard shortcuts Responsive drawers That's where Voyara

22
00:01:12,215 --> 00:01:17,360
comes in. A travel experience that begins with a simple idea and turns it
into a journey

23
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:18,870
designed around you.

24
00:01:19,295 --> 00:01:24,740
Let's plan a trip. Two travellers Kerala December 1st through December 3rd
A relaxed

25
00:01:24,755 --> 00:01:27,250
pace and a budget of ₹200,000.

26
00:01:27,515 --> 00:01:28,950
That's all we need to begin.

27
00:01:30,155 --> 00:01:32,410
The orchestrator assembles the relevant context.

28
00:01:33,075 --> 00:01:34,750
Destination specialists begin their research.

29
00:01:35,335 --> 00:01:38,110
Stay, food and experience specialists contribute their findings.

30
00:01:38,415 --> 00:01:41,250
Then the itinerary and budget agents bring the pieces together.

31
00:01:41,475 --> 00:01:44,730
And all the while, the dashboard and Voyara remain synchronized.

32
00:01:44,995 --> 00:01:47,950
What happens in the application is reflected in the memory dashboard.

33
00:01:48,135 --> 00:01:49,490
The activity is observed.

34
00:01:49,715 --> 00:01:50,940
The model calls are real.

35
00:01:50,955 --> 00:01:54,470
For this demonstration, the waiting time has been accelerated in the edit.

36
00:01:54,995 --> 00:01:56,910
Seven specialists have completed their work.

37
00:01:57,195 --> 00:02:02,370
Voyara now saves the itinerary, indicative costs, and the recorded work of
each agent ready for review.

38
00:02:02,715 --> 00:02:04,630
We open the budget agent's captured context.

39
00:02:04,795 --> 00:02:06,710
There it is, 200,000 rupees.

40
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:10,370
Not just a number, but a requirement supported by a specific claim and its
source.

41
00:02:10,515 --> 00:02:13,230
Here, context allocation is measured using UTF-8 bytes.

42
00:02:13,595 --> 00:02:15,110
So, let's change the budget.

43
00:02:15,335 --> 00:02:18,170
From 200,000 rupees to 120,000.

44
00:02:18,215 --> 00:02:19,340
We save the new requirement.

45
00:02:19,355 --> 00:02:23,070
and before a new plan is generated, the older plan is marked stale.

46
00:02:23,635 --> 00:02:26,510
Now we create a new outline with the same team.

47
00:02:26,835 --> 00:02:29,870
Once again, Voyara and IronWeb move together.

48
00:02:30,155 --> 00:02:32,230
The agents read the revised requirements.

49
00:02:32,495 --> 00:02:35,930
They gather and validate their results against the updated context.

50
00:02:36,275 --> 00:02:38,950
The previous context remains available as history.

51
00:02:39,255 --> 00:02:43,830
The new run captures the revised budget and the evidence that supports the
new plan.

52
00:02:44,175 --> 00:02:48,120
The budget has changed from 200,000 rupees to 120,000.

53
00:02:48,135 --> 00:02:53,710
A new claim has been recorded, a new source supports it, and version 2 is
now current.

54
00:02:54,575 --> 00:02:56,530
Intelligence you can see, memory you can trace,

55
00:02:56,975 --> 00:02:57,770
journeys made personal.
